silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_decomposition_step__step_sigma_enc__rawsource__custodysource__typedterm__admittedterm a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Sigma_enc is the encyclopedia publish signature endofunctor on Set: a recipe that takes any carrier set X and produces a new set Sigma_enc(X). RawSource, CustodySource, TypedTerm, AdmittedTerm are the four sets of typed-term shapes per publish stage. The plus (+) is the disjoint union (coproduct) of these summands. The times (x) is the Cartesian product, pairing a stage carrier with a continuation X. The X is a typed payload that the publish pipeline carries forward at every non-leaf stage." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_decomposition_step__step_sigma_encx__evaluation_of_the_polynomial_endofunctor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The operation Sigma_enc(X) evaluates the polynomial functor at a set X. The result is a tagged disjoint-union: an element of Sigma_enc(X) is either (raw, r) for r in RawSource, or (custody, c, x) for c in CustodySource and x in X, or (type, t, x) for t in TypedTerm and x in X, or (admit, a, x) for a in AdmittedTerm and x in X. The tag identifies which publish stage the element belongs to; the continuation x is the next bind target. The initial algebra of Sigma_enc is the free monad Free(Sigma_enc), the tree of all publish-operation trees." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_decomposition_step__step_polynomial_endofunctor__free_monad_over_a_signature a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats Section 20.4 (free monad on a signature endofunctor) is the categorical base topic. The free monad over a polynomial signature is the colimit of iterated applications Sigma_enc^n; for polynomial signatures over Set the colimit always exists and yields the initial Sigma_enc-algebra. Functional-programming siblings: Meijer-Fokkinga-Paterson 1991 (catamorphisms for initial algebras), Kelly 1980 (transfinite construction of free algebras), the Haskell Functor typeclass." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_decomposition_step__step_mittens_vet_record_polynomial_trace a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Anchor each summand to a concrete Mittens domain witness. The four summands of Sigma_enc become four concrete stages for VetRecord_77 (Mittens annual exam at Tartu Animal Clinic, 2026-05-18, microchip 44B2F9). RawSource = the raw CSV intake at the clinic; CustodySource*X = the same row plus a custody tag and a continuation pointer; TypedTerm*X = the row after type-checking against the EHR schema; AdmittedTerm*X = the row after SHACL validation produces SHACLPassReport_77 and the render produces VetCarePlanPDF_77." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_decomposition_step__step_homsigma_encx__y_iso_product_of_homx__y_per_summand a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By the universal property of coproducts and the definition of exponentials, the Yoneda traversal of Sigma_enc(X) into any set Y splits over the four summands: Hom(Sigma_enc(X), Y) is in bijection with Hom(RawSource, Y) x Hom(CustodySource*X, Y) x Hom(TypedTerm*X, Y) x Hom(AdmittedTerm*X, Y). Downstream every encyclopedia paper inherits this split: paper-19 mereology, paper-15 KG-growth, paper-25 sheaf-gluing each select a different summand-target Y and recover its corresponding hom-set." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_decomposition_step__step_sigma_enc_polynomial_form_recap a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Sigma_enc is the four-summand polynomial endofunctor on Set whose initial algebra is the free monad Free(Sigma_enc). The summands are RawSource (constant), CustodySource*X (custody-bind), TypedTerm*X (type-bind), AdmittedTerm*X (admit-bind). Every Mittens publish trace is one term in Free(Sigma_enc); every downstream paper Yoneda-reads from this signature without rewriting it." .
